---
/**
 * TEMPORARY TEST FIXTURE — /temp/fake_campaign
 *
 * Fictional campaign page for a fictional candidacy, used to exercise the
 * candidate campaign-URL pipeline end to end: portal submission →
 * campaignscraper → Gemini values scoring → candidate_campaign_details →
 * the candidate's implied beliefs in the app.
 *
 * Delete this file and the `/temp/` sitemap exclusion in astro.config.mjs
 * when campaign-URL testing is finished.
 *
 * ── Why this page does NOT use BaseLayout ────────────────────────────────
 *
 * BaseLayout renders the site header, whose nav links to /, /about,
 * /insights, /faq and /donate. campaignscraper crawls to MaxDepth 2 and
 * MaxPages 25 within the same eTLD+1, so a single nav would pull the entire
 * marketing site into the scrape and the candidate's "implied beliefs" would
 * be extracted partly from Voxivium's own copy. A campaign page must be an
 * island for the scrape to mean anything.
 *
 * That is also why there is not one internal link anywhere below — no nav,
 * no footer, no cross-links (CEO 2026-09-01). Anything added here that
 * points at another voxivium.com page silently changes what this test
 * measures.
 *
 * ── Why it is labelled as fictional in visible copy ──────────────────────
 *
 * This is a real domain serving what reads as a real congressional campaign.
 * The banner and the closing note are what keep a visitor who arrives by
 * accident from mistaking it for one. noindex keeps it out of search; the
 * banner covers everyone the noindex does not.
 *
 * The label costs a little scrape fidelity — the evaluator sees it — but it
 * states no policy position, so it does not compete with the fifteen that
 * follow.
 *
 * ── Content shape ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 *
 * Fifteen of the twenty belief domains, one section each, each taking a
 * position concrete enough to score. The five deliberately omitted are
 * Foreign Policy, Technology, Agriculture & Rural, Financial Regulation and
 * Federalism — absent so the run can be checked for correctly reporting NO
 * coverage rather than inventing it, which is the harder half to verify.
 *
 * The persona is a mainstream Democrat with two deliberate crossovers
 * (border enforcement, defense readiness) so the alignment output is not
 * uniformly one direction and the "most misaligned" surfaces have something
 * to show against a Democratic-leaning district.
 */
import '@styles/global.css'

const canonical = 'https://voxivium.com/temp/fake_campaign'

/** One section per belief domain covered. Order is presentation order. */
const positions: { heading: string; body: string[] }[] = [
  {
    heading: 'Jobs, Wages and the Cost of Living',
    body: [
      'Working families in Burlington and Ocean counties are running harder to stay in the same place. I support raising the federal minimum wage to $17 an hour, indexed to inflation so Congress stops relitigating it every decade, and making the expanded Child Tax Credit permanent.',
      'I will vote to raise the top marginal rate and to close the carried-interest loophole. A tax code that asks a warehouse supervisor in Willingboro to pay a higher effective rate than a hedge fund partner is not a tax code anyone should defend.',
    ],
  },
  {
    heading: 'Health Care',
    body: [
      'Health care is a right, not a product. I support a public option available on every exchange in the country, permanent expansion of ACA premium subsidies, and a $35 monthly cap on insulin for everyone — not only for seniors on Medicare.',
      'Medicare should negotiate the price of every drug it buys, not a short list. I will oppose any budget that reaches savings by narrowing eligibility.',
    ],
  },
  {
    heading: 'Social Security and the Safety Net',
    body: [
      "I will not vote to raise the retirement age or to means-test benefits people already paid for. Social Security's shortfall is a revenue problem, and I support lifting the payroll tax cap on income above $400,000 to close it.",
      'I support permanent paid family and medical leave at the federal level, and protecting SNAP from work-requirement expansions that cut people off for paperwork rather than for need.',
    ],
  },
  {
    heading: 'Veterans and National Defense',
    body: [
      'This district is home to Joint Base McGuire-Dix-Lakehurst, and readiness is not an abstraction here. I support sustaining force readiness and a pay raise for junior enlisted servicemembers, and I will not vote for a budget that hollows out the base.',
      'Supporting the military and auditing it are the same commitment. The Pentagon has never passed a clean audit. I will vote to keep defense spending strong and to make passing that audit a condition of future increases.',
    ],
  },
  {
    heading: 'Immigration and the Border',
    body: [
      'Border security and immigrant dignity are not opposites, and I am tired of being told to choose. I support more immigration judges to clear the asylum backlog, modern screening technology at ports of entry, and the additional enforcement personnel the bipartisan border bill funded.',
      'In the same bill I will vote for a path to citizenship for Dreamers and for farm and hospitality workers who have been here for years, paying taxes, raising children who are citizens. A system that can neither remove nor legalize anyone is the actual crisis.',
    ],
  },
  {
    heading: 'Criminal Justice',
    body: [
      "Our system should be measured by whether people come out less likely to reoffend. I support ending cash bail for non-violent offenses, expanding federal reentry and job-training programs, and repealing mandatory minimums that tie a judge's hands.",
      'I support funding police departments properly and pairing that with real accountability: a national misconduct registry so an officer fired in one state cannot be quietly rehired in another.',
    ],
  },
  {
    heading: 'Civil Rights',
    body: [
      'I support passing the Equality Act to extend federal anti-discrimination protection in housing, employment and public accommodation to LGBTQ Americans, and restoring the preclearance requirements the Supreme Court struck from the Voting Rights Act.',
      'Federal enforcement exists because leaving these questions to the states produced exactly the outcomes it was created to correct.',
    ],
  },
  {
    heading: 'Privacy and Civil Liberties',
    body: [
      "I will vote against reauthorizing warrantless surveillance of Americans' communications, and I support closing the data-broker loophole that lets federal agencies purchase location data they would need a warrant to collect directly.",
      'A warrant requirement is not an obstacle to law enforcement. It is the price of doing it in a free country.',
    ],
  },
  {
    heading: 'Environment and Energy',
    body: [
      'I support the clean energy tax credits, a binding federal target of net-zero electricity by 2035, and stronger EPA authority over PFAS contamination — which is not theoretical in this district.',
      'The transition has to bring refinery and utility workers with it. I will not support a climate bill that has no wage-replacement and retraining guarantee for the workers whose jobs it ends.',
    ],
  },
  {
    heading: 'Education',
    body: [
      'I support doubling Title I funding, universal pre-K, and raising the federal share of special-education costs to the 40% Congress promised in 1975 and has never once delivered.',
      'I oppose diverting public money to private-school vouchers. Federal dollars belong in the public schools that are required to accept every child who walks through the door.',
    ],
  },
  {
    heading: 'Gun Safety',
    body: [
      'I support universal background checks, federal red-flag legislation with due-process protections, and restoring the assault weapons ban. Ninety percent of Americans support background checks and Congress has not acted.',
      'None of this touches lawful hunting or home defense, and I will say so to anyone who claims otherwise.',
    ],
  },
  {
    heading: 'Personal Freedom',
    body: [
      'I will vote to codify Roe v. Wade into federal law. The decision belongs to a woman and her doctor, not to a congressman.',
      "I support protecting access to contraception and IVF by statute, and I will oppose any federal effort to write one religious tradition's conclusions into everyone's law.",
    ],
  },
  {
    heading: 'Workers and Unions',
    body: [
      'I support the PRO Act, banning captive-audience meetings, and real penalties for employers who fire workers for organizing — penalties large enough to stop being a line item.',
      'I support extending overtime protection to salaried workers up to $75,000 and ending the misclassification of full-time employees as independent contractors.',
    ],
  },
  {
    heading: 'Housing',
    body: [
      'The shortage is a supply problem and it will not fix itself locally. I support a federal housing production fund tied to zoning reform, expanding the Low-Income Housing Tax Credit, and full funding for Section 8 vouchers so the program stops turning away eligible families.',
      'I support down-payment assistance for first-time buyers and limits on large investment firms buying single-family homes in bulk.',
    ],
  },
  {
    heading: 'Democracy and Government Reform',
    body: [
      'I support the Freedom to Vote Act, automatic voter registration, an end to partisan gerrymandering through independent commissions, and overturning Citizens United by constitutional amendment.',
      'I support a total ban on individual stock trading by members of Congress and their spouses. If you cannot serve without trading on what you learn in a briefing, do not serve.',
    ],
  },
]
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>Bob Seamon for Congress — New Jersey's 3rd District</title>
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="Fictional test campaign page. Bob Seamon for U.S. House of Representatives, New Jersey's 3rd Congressional District — where the candidate stands."
    />
    <link rel="canonical" href={canonical} />
    <!-- Not a real campaign, and not to be indexed or followed. -->
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow" />
  </head>

  <body class="bg-white text-slate-900 antialiased">
    <div role="note" class="border-b-4 border-amber-500 bg-amber-100 px-6 py-4 text-amber-950">
      <p class="mx-auto max-w-3xl text-sm leading-relaxed font-semibold">
        TEST PAGE — FICTIONAL CONTENT. This page was created by Voxivium to test its
        campaign-analysis software. Bob Seamon is not a candidate for any office, is not running for
        Congress, and none of the statements below is a real campaign position. Nothing here should
        be relied on by voters.
      </p>
    </div>

    <header class="border-b border-slate-200 bg-slate-900 px-6 py-14 text-white">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
        <p class="text-sm font-semibold tracking-[0.2em] text-sky-300 uppercase">
          Seamon for Congress
        </p>
        <h1 class="mt-3 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-5xl">Bob Seamon</h1>
        <p class="mt-3 text-xl text-slate-300">Candidate for the U.S. House of Representatives</p>
        <p class="text-lg text-slate-400">New Jersey's 3rd Congressional District</p>
        <p class="mt-8 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-slate-200">
          I am running because this district deserves a representative who will tell you exactly
          where he stands before you vote, not after. Every position I hold is on this page. Read
          them, and hold me to them.
        </p>
      </div>
    </header>

    <main class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-14">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight">Where I Stand</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-lg text-slate-600">
        Fifteen issues, stated plainly. Where I break with my own party, I have said so.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-12 space-y-12">
        {
          positions.map((position) => (
            <section>
              <h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-slate-900">
                {position.heading}
              </h3>
              {position.body.map((paragraph) => (
                <p class="mt-4 text-lg leading-relaxed text-slate-700">{paragraph}</p>
              ))}
            </section>
          ))
        }
      </div>

      <section class="mt-16 border-t border-slate-200 pt-10">
        <h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">About Bob</h3>
        <p class="mt-4 text-lg leading-relaxed text-slate-700">
          Bob Seamon is a fictional candidate. In this fiction he has lived in Burlington County for
          twenty-two years, spent his career in software, served two terms on a local school board,
          and is married with three children.
        </p>
      </section>

      <p class="mt-16 rounded-lg bg-slate-100 p-6 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
        <strong class="font-semibold text-slate-800">Reminder:</strong> this is a fictional page published
        by Voxivium solely to test automated analysis of candidate campaign websites. It is not a campaign
        communication, it is not authorized by any candidate or committee, and no donations are solicited
        or accepted.
      </p>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
